From d811b68a1086fda5300d346999df2b4d8b7fb891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abinash Haldorai <abinash.haldorai@eka.care>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:36:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Voice: make a phone call a recorded conversation

A finished phone call was invisible to the console. The Conversations page
lists sessions from the DynamoDB session table, and the console's ingest
drops message rows whose session row is missing ("not in dynamo"); chat
writes that row on the first user message, but the voice pipeline never did,
so a call's transcript was saved with no session to hang it on.

- /voice/answer sessions now have channel "voice" (the name the console's
  channel filter already offers).
- When the call connects, mark_conversation_initiated writes the session row,
  the same call chat makes on the first message.
- When the call ends, call_record merges what only the pipeline knows into
  the session's initial_context under "call": duration, how it ended
  (caller_hung_up, silence, time_limit, transferred, error), caller turns,
  handover outcome (none, requested, transferred, failed, declined), tools
  used, and the caller's number masked. The session's other context is kept.
  It is best effort: a failure is logged, never raised.
- The agent processor notes the names of tools the agent calls; the handover
  tool and processor record their outcome on the shared HandoverState.

The browser (WebRTC) voice pipeline has the same gap and is not changed
here.

Not run on a real call: the end-of-call wiring in the pipeline (disconnect,
silence, time limit handlers) is a few lines and is not covered by a test;
the record itself, the tool-name capture and the outcomes are.

